{"id":"000W1S","title":"Triage Route (Infections)","author":"gdc","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-14T19:15:20+00:00","posted":"Heute, 19:42 Uhr","rules":"Episode 6 of the Norma L. Dokes series. It was originally supposed to be a liar (Yajisan-Kazusan) puzzle, but I decided to release a Yajilin first because the liar turned out very hard. It introduces concepts for next week's liar-episode. According to testers (thanks everyone!) difficulty should be around 3.5 stars. Enjoy!\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nInfection Sources: Each digit matching its box number is an \"infection source\". Each row and column contains an infection source. They are infected.\n\nTransmission: Infected cells infect all smaller orthogonal neighbors. This process repeats until no further infections are possible.\n\nCircles: A digit in a circle indicates the total number of infected cells along all indicated directions. Circle cells must remain uninfected.\n\nYajilin: Draw an orthogonal loop. The loop passes through all and only uninfected cells (also circles).\n\nClick on the image to play!\n\n(Bad) Example Puzzle\n\nA 6x6 puzzle with the same rules except the loop is branching and not closed because I couldn't make it work (sorry). Colors: orange for infection sources, red for secondary infections and green for uninfected.","solutionCode":"Infected Cells in column 7, top to bottom (up to 9 digits).","tags":["Sudoku","Yajilin","Fortress (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/opchzga3sa","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/normaldokes","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/opchzga3sa","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-14T19:15:20+00:00"}